# Writing room buttons

**NEVER** use "Room occupied", "Occupied", or any occupied-state label as a **button** label — on Android, web, or anywhere else.

Allowed writing-room **button** labels only:
- Enter room / Enter writing room
- Exit room / Exit writing room
- Entering writing room / Exiting writing room (or Leaving…) while a transition is in progress

Occupied state is communicated with a **dialog/message** when the user tries to enter (or on open), never by renaming the button.

```
// ❌ BAD — button text changes when someone else holds the room
button.text = "Room occupied"

// ✅ GOOD — button stays Enter; tap shows Occupied dialog
button.text = "Enter writing room"
// → show "Room occupied" dialog / alert
```

Also: no ASCII `| / - \` rotators on the Android app — ever.
